course: dictionary
lesson: 612
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word axe can be a tool for chopping wood, or it can mean to end something suddenly. «The bus route was axed» is about cancelling, not a tool, because a bus route cannot be chopped with a blade.
explain: Ask yourself what fits. «The woodcutter swung his axe at the log» is about a tool, because a woodcutter uses a tool for chopping. «The TV show was axed after one series» means it was stopped suddenly. The words around the word give you the clues.
explain: Some words are used in set phrases, where the meaning is not the literal one. «Have an axe to grind» means you have a private reason, often a grudge, for doing or saying something. You cannot work this out by thinking about a real axe, so learn it as a phrase.
fact: An axe is a tool with a heavy metal blade on a long handle, used for chopping wood or cutting down trees.
fact: «Axe» can also be a verb: to axe something means to cut it or end it suddenly.
fact: Informal: to axe workers means to sack them or make them lose their jobs.
fact: «Have an axe to grind» means to have a private reason, often a grudge.
fact: «Ötzi the Iceman» lived about 5,300 years ago and carried a copper axe. He was found by hikers in 1991.
exercise: «The woodcutter swung his axe and split the log in two.» What is an axe in this sentence? | *A tool with a heavy metal blade for chopping wood | A loud noise | A long walk | A kind of bird
exercise: «The council axed the bus route to save money.» What does axed mean? | Painted a bright colour | *Cancelled or cut suddenly | Chopped down with a tool | Lost in the snow
exercise: Maya says, «He has an axe to grind with his brother.» What does this suggest? | *He has a private reason, often a grudge, against his brother | He is going to chop wood | He wants to play with a toy axe | He is very happy with his brother
test: «Workers were axed when the factory closed.» What does axed suggest here? | *They lost their jobs | They were painted blue | They built a new factory | They went on holiday
test: «Ötzi the Iceman had a copper axe.» What metal was his axe made of? | *Copper | Stone | Iron | Gold
exam: «The TV show was axed after one series.» What does axed mean here? | Filmed outdoors in the rain | Chopped with a heavy blade | *Cancelled suddenly | Repeated many times
